# AuthSentinel

AuthSentinel is a Python project I built to practice log analysis and learn more about defensive cybersecurity.

The program reads login records from a text file and analyzes successful and failed login attempts.

## What it does

- Counts successful and failed logins.
- Tracks failed attempts by IP address.
- Tracks failed attempts by username.
- Checks whether two failed attempts from the same IP happened within 60 seconds.
- Gives each user a basic risk level based on failed attempts.
- Prints a report with the collected results.

## Built with

- Python
- datetime
- Dictionaries and Lists
- File Handling

## Log Format

Each log entry should contain:

```text
username,status,ip_address,timestamp
```

Example:

```text
ahmad,FAILED,192.168.1.10,2026-10-31 20:10:00
sara,SUCCESS,192.168.1.15,2026-10-31 20:12:00
ahmad,FAILED,192.168.1.10,2026-10-31 20:13:00
```

## Run the project

```bash
python main.py
```

## Note

This is a learning project. The risk levels are based only on failed login counts and do not prove that an account or IP address is malicious.

All testing should use sample logs or data you are authorized to analyze.

